# tutorials
# `checkpoints` and `outputs` are Hydra / training artifact dirs. Bare (un-
# anchored) so they're ignored at any depth: a tutorial's checkpoint_dir and
# hydra.run.dir are relative to the launch cwd, so running from the repo root
# vs. from inside tutorials/<name>/ (e.g. an IDE run) lands them at different
# nesting levels — a bare rule catches them all.
checkpoints
outputs/

# graphviz's render() writes the DOT source alongside the .svg, with no
# extension (tutorials/iris/iris_model, .../iris_pruned_model, ...). Ignore
# those build artifacts; the rendered *.svg diagrams are kept, since the
# pattern only matches names *ending* in _model.
tutorials/*/*_model

tutorials/concrete/outputs
tutorials/concrete/data
tutorials/iris/outputs
tutorials/california_housing/outputs
tutorials/otto/data
tutorials/otto/outputs
tutorials/ccpp/data
tutorials/ccpp/outputs


